      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/10e6b2c714e219e304df928978bf116266a33308",
      "actor": null,
      "commit_id": null,
      "commit_url": null,
      "created_at": null,
      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/10e6b2c714e219e304df928978bf116266a33308",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "5d2d8a23f603c42c9d4a7f4dddbcf60fceb741ca",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/5d2d8a23f603c42c9d4a7f4dddbcf60fceb741ca"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 5d2d8a23f603c42c9d4a7f4dddbcf60fceb741ca\nparent 89307c49609f331505573985b8a081fea49a3d07\nauthor Lőrinc <pap.lorinc@gmail.com> 1788747029 -0700\ncommitter Hodlinator <172445034+hodlinator@users.noreply.github.com> 1788787637 +0200\n\nhttp: fail closed on partial binds\n\nWhen any RPC bind succeeds, initialization ignores every other endpoint failure. A process that already owns the default IPv4 port can therefore receive bitcoin-cli credentials while the node continues on IPv6.\n\nDeduplicate equivalent endpoints, require every distinct default or explicit endpoint to bind, and close partial listeners on failure. Hosts intentionally providing one address family must select that endpoint explicitly.\n\nThis carries the fail-closed policy from bitcoin/bitcoin#14968 now that the in-tree socket implementation reports each bind result.\n\nCo-authored-by: laanwj <126646+laanwj@users.noreply.github.com>\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg39Hzirivn9mM3G8qwAOGOKsmHT\ny2f/O2iDRQI8UxEyoAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCXvE2R5jXWkAudd1PJGufYHkTHYF4omZMqPr3VExlJlwICJpW9NXd889A9FPSoybr\ncJy6s1GowWTZ1uhO15IwE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
      },
      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/89307c49609f331505573985b8a081fea49a3d07",
          "sha": "89307c49609f331505573985b8a081fea49a3d07",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/89307c49609f331505573985b8a081fea49a3d07"
        }
      ],
      "message": "http: fail closed on partial binds\n\nWhen any RPC bind succeeds, initialization ignores every other endpoint failure. A process that already owns the default IPv4 port can therefore receive bitcoin-cli credentials while the node continues on IPv6.\n\nDeduplicate equivalent endpoints, require every distinct default or explicit endpoint to bind, and close partial listeners on failure. Hosts intentionally providing one address family must select that endpoint explicitly.\n\nThis carries the fail-closed policy from bitcoin/bitcoin#14968 now that the in-tree socket implementation reports each bind result.\n\nCo-authored-by: laanwj <126646+laanwj@users.noreply.github.com>",
      "committer": {
